# AutoSign fills the sign editor's own text buffer rather than simulating keystrokes into it. The
# buffer is what removed() reads to build ServerboundSignUpdatePacket, so writing it directly is
# writing exactly what vanilla would have sent -- there is no separate "our text" path to get out of
# step with the packet. `text` and `sign` are also needed so the on-screen preview matches the
# buffer; without them the screen would show a blank sign and then send four filled lines.
#
# Widened rather than mixed into because there is no behaviour to change here, only fields to read.
# A mixin would be four @Accessor methods saying the same thing at more cost.
